      'One prominent expression is the reinterpretation of historic Pietra Dura (parchin kari) stone inlay traditions. Rather than covering entire surfaces with elaborate floral motifs, contemporary designers use laser-cut brass, lapis lazuli, malachite, or mother-of-pearl strips inlaid into minimalist Italian marble dining tables, master bathroom vanity backsplashes, or entrance foyer feature panels.',
